From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: setup offers two ways to start, Default and Minimal

Dresden, 2026-10-20: two experiences, not three, and the Google one goes
(docs/setup-experiences.md, vision.md "Setup's experiences").

- Default, preselected: DuckDuckGo searches the web from the browser and
  the launcher, and Proton's apps (Mail, Calendar, Drive, Docs, Pass, VPN,
  Lumo) are bookmarked, in a Proton folder on the bookmarks bar.
- Minimal: the launcher searches only the device, nothing else is set up.

Under the two, the screen says what comes either way: Bazaar, and the apps
that open photos, videos, music and documents (nickel-flatpak's first-boot
apps). The copy is plainer: "How would you like to start?".

The choice is stored as "default" or "minimal"; "privacy", from builds
before this, counts as Default. uBlock Origin, the rest of Default, comes
with its own patch (Manifest V2 kept, its package and updates from
NickelOS).

